card.statement:
For any cuspidal $\V$-module $M$ there exists $N \in \N$ such that for all $p, q \in \Z^m$, $r \in \{0,1\}^n$, $i, j = 1,\ldots, m$, $\alpha = 1, \ldots, n$, the following elements of $U(\V)$ annihilate $M$:

\begin{align}
&\sum_{a=0}^N (-1)^a {N \choose a} (t^{p} t_i^a \xi^r d_j) (t_i^{q-a} d_i), \\
&\sum_{a=0}^N (-1)^a {N \choose a} (t^{p} t_i^a \xi^r \pd_\alpha) (t_i^{q-a} d_i), \\
&\sum_{a=0}^N (-1)^a {N \choose a} (t^{p} t_i^a \xi^r d_0) (t_i^{q-a} d_i).
\end{align}
